  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the primary uncertainty is what the baseline performance looks like and which modality/architecture choices matter. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most standard configuration in the space: it uses a well-understood linear encoder (PCA), the simplest profile setting, and isolates the RNA signal without confounding from image features, complex aggregation, or fusion. Establishing this baseline is essential before interpreting any multimodal or image-only result, because it tells us (a) how much signal RNA alone carries, (b) the performance floor, and (c) how much headroom exists for the image modality or more complex architectures to exploit. Under a limited budget, this single experiment reduces the most uncertainty per trial by anchoring the entire comparison space."
}

